:: Bedroom Robin Wrap
<<effects>><<wearProp "giftbox">>
<<switch $christmas_gift_robin>>
	<<case "shirt">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's shirt and shorts. You wrap them as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
	<<case "sundress">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's sundress. You wrap it as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
	<<case "kimono">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's kimono. You wrap it as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
	<<case "tuxedo">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's tuxedo. You wrap it as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
	<<case "gothic gown">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's gothic gown. You wrap it as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
	<<case "christmas">>
		With the wrapping paper and marker in hand, you prepare Robin's Christmas outfit. You wrap it as carefully as you can. The gift has a fetching look to it once done, with Robin's name scrawled across one surface.
<</switch>>
<br><br>

You carry the gift out to the main hall and tuck it beneath the plastic tree, where the lights cast weak little colours across the wrapping paper.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Bedroom Orphans Clothes Wrap
<<effects>><<wearProp "giftbox">>

You spend a lot of time sorting through the clothes, deciding who gets what. There are a lot of orphans, and you don't know them all that well, but you think you can guess their sizes.
<br><br>

Once wrapped, you make several round trips to the plastic tree in the main hall. You leave the gifts stacked in neat piles.
<br><br>

You find a piece of tape stuck to your nose.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Widgets Orphanage Christmas [widget]
<<widget "christmas_robin_visit">>
	<<if $robinmissing isnot 0>>
		Your eyes turn to your bedroom door, as if expecting a visitor. But no one's there.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 60>>
		You hear knocking on your door. But no one enters. You peek outside, and find a small object wrapped in tinfoil. There's a note attached.
		<br><br>
		"Merry Christmas. <span class="gold">I left something for you under the tree.</span>" - Robin
		<br><br>

		You unwrap the object. There's a cookie inside. It's doughy and sweet.<<ltrauma>><<lstress>><<trauma -6>><<stress -6>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 20>>
		<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
		You hear a knock on your door. Robin pokes <<his>> head around the corner. "Is it okay if I come in?"
		<br><br>

		<<He>> enters. <<He>> looks exhausted. "Merry Christmas. The orphans are celebrating. <span class="gold">I left you something under the tree.</span>" <<He>> tries to smile, then places a small object wrapped in tinfoil on your bed. "You should join us when you're ready."
		<br><br>

		<<He>> leaves the room. You unwrap the object. There's a cookie inside. It's doughy and sweet.<<ltrauma>><<lstress>><<trauma -6>><<stress -6>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>

	<<else>>
		<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
		You hear a flurry of knocks on your door. Robin pokes <<his>> head inside. "Can I come in?"
		<br><br>

		"Merry Christmas!" <<he>> says as soon as you answer, bright enough to fill the room. <<He>> crosses to your bed and sets down a small bundle wrapped in tinfoil. "The orphans hung up decorations. They're celebrating! You should join us."
		<br><br>

		"Oh, and," <<he>> adds, turning back at the door, <span class="gold">"I left you something under the tree!"</span>
		<br><br>

		<<if $robinromance is 1>>
			<<He>> squeezes your hand, kisses your cheek, and slips back into the hall with a grin that lingers after <<hes>> gone.
		<<else>>
			<<He>> darts back out into the hall, too full of energy to stand still for long.
		<</if>>
		You unwrap the foil and find a soft cookie inside, slightly squashed and far sweeter than it has any right to be.<<ltrauma>><<lstress>><<trauma -6>><<stress -6>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "christmas_robin">>
	<<npc Robin>><<person1>><<generatey2>><<person2>>
	Robin has spent most of the day keeping an eye on the younger orphans. A <<person>> tugs at <<person1>><<his>> sleeve and holds out a gift. "It's not from me," the <<person2>><<person>> says. "I just found it under the tree."
	<br><br>

	Robin thanks the <<person>> and <<person1>>turns the parcel over in <<his>> hands. <<He>> spots your handwriting almost at once, and the look on <<his>> face softens.
	<br><br>

	<<switch $christmas_gift_robin>>
		<<case "shirt">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftShirt">>
		<<case "sundress">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftSundress">>
		<<case "kimono">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftKimono">>
		<<case "tuxedo">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftTux">>
		<<case "gothic gown">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftGown">>
		<<case "christmas">><<set _robinPush to "robinGiftChristmas">>
	<</switch>>

	<<if $christmas_gift_robin is undefined>>
	<<elseif C.npc.Robin.outfits is undefined>>
		<<set C.npc.Robin.outfits = [_robinPush]>>
	<<else>>
		<<run C.npc.Robin.outfits.pushUnique(_robinPush)>>
	<</if>>

	<<speechresolve>>

	<<if (($christmas_gift_robin is "shirt") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m")) or (($christmas_gift_robin is "sundress") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f"))>>
		Excited, <<he>> tears into the wrapping paper. <<His>> whole face lights up when <<he>> sees the clothes inside, and <<he>> hugs them to <<his>> chest as though someone might snatch them away.<<ltrauma>><<trauma -6>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			"I love it!" <<he>> says. "Thank you so much." <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and leans in close enough for only you to hear. <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> slips away down one of the halls towards <<his>> room, glancing back at you with a grin.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			"I love it!" <<he>> says. "Thank you so much." <<He>> hugs the gift again, then hurries off down one of the halls towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif (($christmas_gift_robin is "shirt") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f")) or (($christmas_gift_robin is "sundress") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m"))>>

		Excited, <<he>> tears off the wrapping paper. <<His>> bright expression turns to confusion as <<he>> pulls out the clothing.
		<br><br>

		"I-I think you may have given me the wrong present," <<he>> says, voice small with uncertainty. "This is for <<if C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m">>girls<<else>>boys<</if>>, isn't it?"
		<br><br>

		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
			You duck your head. "I-I just thought it would suit you."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			You look anywhere but at <<him>>. "I thought you might look nice in it, that's all."
		<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
			"I chose it because I thought it would suit you," you say.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
			"I only wanted to give you something that felt right for you," you say gently.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
			"It is. Try it on, and you'll see what I mean."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
			"Try it first," you say. "Then tell me I was wrong."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"You'd do well to trust my eye," you say. "It would look better on you than whatever excuse you were wearing before."
		<<else>>
			"I thought you'd look cute in it," you say.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			Robin's eyes brighten. "Really? Th-thank you." <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and whispers close to your ear, <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> disappears down one of the halls with the bundle clutched tight against <<his>> chest.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif C.npc.Robin.love gte 40 or $robinromance is 1>>
			Robin seems embarrassed, but not upset. "Th-thanks, I guess. I'll be sure to wear it!" <<He>> disappears down one of the halls, towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			Robin looks conflicted. "I-I appreciate the thought. Thank you." <<He>> folds the clothes up, and returns to <<his>> room.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
		<<if C.npc.Robin.crossdress is undefined>>
			<<set C.npc.Robin.crossdress to 1>>
		<</if>>
		<<if C.npc.Robin.cdstart is undefined>>
			<<set C.npc.Robin.cdstart to "christmas">>
		<</if>>

	<<elseif $christmas_gift_robin is "kimono">>
		Excited, <<he>> tears off the wrapping paper. <<He>> smiles when <<he>> sees the fabric, then slows as <<he>> pulls the kimono free and feels its weight in <<his>> hands. You caught <<him>> off guard.
		<br><br>
		"T-this isn't a costume," <<he>> says, unfolding the kimono with care. "How much did you spend on this?"
		<br><br>

		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
			You give a small shrug. "N-not too much. I just wanted to get you something special."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			Your mouth twitches. "I saw it and thought of you."
		<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
			"Enough," you say. "You were worth the trouble."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
			"Don't worry about the cost," you say softly. "I wanted you to have it."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
			"More than I should have, maybe," you say, "but it's yours now."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
			"Stop fussing and enjoy it," you say. "You look good in nice things."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Enough to make sure you had something decent for once," you say.
		<<else>>
			You shrug. "I wanted to spoil you a bit."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			Robin draws the fabric close, smiling before <<he>> can quite stop <<himself>>. "It's so pretty. Thank you so much." <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and whispers, <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> slips away down one of the halls with the kimono held tight.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			Robin runs <<his>> fingers over the cloth once more. "It's so pretty. Thank you so much." <<He>> hugs it to <<his>> chest and heads off towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif (($christmas_gift_robin is "tuxedo") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m")) or (($christmas_gift_robin is "gothic gown") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f"))>>
		Excited, <<he>> tears off the wrapping paper. <<He>> smiles at first, then gulps when <<he>> sees what is really inside. The care <<he>> takes unfolding it only makes it look pricier.
		<br><br>
		"T-this isn't a costume," <<he>> says, spreading the <<print (($christmas_gift_robin is "tuxedo") ? "tuxedo" : "gothic gown")>> out with both hands. "How much did you spend on this? This looks really expensive."
		<br><br>

		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
			You fidget with your sleeve. "I just wanted you to have something lovely."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			You glance down. "I couldn't help picturing you in it."
		<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
			"It suited you the moment I saw it," you say.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
			"You deserve nice things too," you say, keeping your voice gentle.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
			"Enough," you say. "And it was worth every penny."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
			"More than you need to know," you say. "Just wear it for me."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Enough to drag your wardrobe out of the gutter," you say.
		<<else>>
			You smile. "Think of it as an investment."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			"It's beautiful. I can't wait for you to see me in it," Robin says. <<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 80>>"Or help me take it off."<<else>>"Thank you so much."<</if>> <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and whispers, <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> vanishes down one of the halls with a smile <<he>> cannot quite hide.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			"It's beautiful. I can't wait for you to see me in it," Robin says. "Thank you so much." <<He>> gathers it against <<his>> chest and hurries back towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif (($christmas_gift_robin is "tuxedo") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "f")) or (($christmas_gift_robin is "gothic gown") and (C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m"))>>
		Excited, <<he>> tears off the wrapping paper. <<He>> smiles when <<he>> first sees the fabric, then frowns as <<he>> pulls it free and realises what you've actually bought.
		<br><br>
		"T-this isn't a costume," <<he>> says, unfolding the <<print (($christmas_gift_robin is "tuxedo") ? "tuxedo" : "gothic gown")>> with care. "How much did you spend on this?"
		<br><br>
		"Wait! Don't answer that yet." <<He>> looks from the clothes to you, clearly trying to make sense of it all. "This is for <<if C.npc.Robin.pronoun is "m">>girls<<else>>boys<</if>>, isn't it?"
		<br><br>

		<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek")>>
			"I-I thought it would suit you," you admit.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
			You rub at your arm. "I kept thinking about how you'd look in it."
		<<elseif ((_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite") or (_speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant"))>>
			"I chose it because I thought it would suit you," you say.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
			"I wanted to give you something that fit the way I see you," you say softly.
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "confident")>>
			"Yes," you say. "And I was right to."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty")>>
			"Obviously," you say. "Try it on before you complain."
		<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
			"Yes," you say. "It would still suit you better than pretending otherwise."
		<<else>>
			"I thought you'd look cute in it," you say.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			Robin's eyes brighten at once. "Really? Th-thank you." <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and whispers, <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> disappears down one of the halls with the gift clasped to <<his>> chest.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif (C.npc.Robin.love gte 40) or ($robinromance is 1)>>
			Robin flushes, but <<he>> does not look upset. "Th-thanks. I'll wear it." <<He>> folds the clothing carefully and heads back towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			Robin looks conflicted. "I-I appreciate the thought. Thank you." <<He>> folds the clothes up, and returns to <<his>> room.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<if C.npc.Robin.crossdress is undefined>>
			<<set C.npc.Robin.crossdress to 1>>
		<</if>>
		<<if C.npc.Robin.cdstart is undefined>>
			<<set C.npc.Robin.cdstart to "christmas">>
		<</if>>

	<<else>>
		Excited, <<he>> tears into the wrapping paper. <<His>> smile grows wider and wider as the festive outfit emerges, until <<hes>> hugging it close with a little laugh.<<ltrauma>><<trauma -6>>
		<br><br>

		<<if (($robinromance is 1) or ($robinsexfriend is 1)) and (C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40)>>
			<<set $christmas_robin_lewd to 1>>
			"I love it!" <<he>> says. "It's so festive. Thank you so much." <<He>> throws <<his>> arms around you and whispers, <span class="gold">"Meet me in my room."</span>
			<br><br>
			<<He>> slips away down one of the halls, grinning over <<his>> shoulder.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			"I love it!" <<he>> says. "It's so festive. Thank you so much." <<He>> clutches it to <<his>> chest and hurries back towards <<his>> room.<<ggglove>><<npcincr Robin love 10>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Next|Orphanage]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</widget>>
